{"id":"3e88eaec4442b96a","group":"58","path":"58/batch07/58-df-twin-prime.md","title":"Twin Primes","display":"df-twin-prime — Twin Primes","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-twin-prime","aliases":["58-df-twin-prime","Twin Primes"],"display":"df-twin-prime — Twin Primes","depends_on":["[[../batch20/58-df-prime.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-twin-prime"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-twin-prime</span><span>Twin Primes</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-twin-prime — Twin Primes"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"3322615e4eea05e9\" href=\"?note=3322615e4eea05e9\" title=\"../batch20/58-df-prime.md\">../batch20/58-df-prime.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p,q\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(p,q\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span> (number candidates)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Prime}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{Prime}_S\\)</span> (prime predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"3322615e4eea05e9\" href=\"?note=3322615e4eea05e9\" title=\"../batch20/58-df-prime.md\">../batch20/58-df-prime.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{TwinPrimePair}_S(p,q)\">\\(\\operatorname{TwinPrimePair}_S(p,q)\\)</span> (twin-prime-pair predicate defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi_2(x)\">\\(\\pi_2(x)\\)</span> (twin-prime counting function defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"C_2\">\\(C_2\\)</span> (twin-prime constant defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{HardyLittlewoodTwinPrimeAsymptotic}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{HardyLittlewoodTwinPrimeAsymptotic}_S\\)</span> (asymptotic predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}twin\\text{-}prime\\text{-}pair} \\vdash \\operatorname{TwinPrimePair}_S(p,q)\\leftrightarrow p,q\\in\\mathbb N\\land\\operatorname{Prime}_S(p)\\land\\operatorname{Prime}_S(q)\\land q=p+2\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}twin\\text{-}prime\\text{-}pair} \\vdash \\operatorname{TwinPrimePair}_S(p,q)\\leftrightarrow p,q\\in\\mathbb N\\land\\operatorname{Prime}_S(p)\\land\\operatorname{Prime}_S(q)\\land q=p+2\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}twin\\text{-}prime\\text{-}count} \\vdash \\forall x\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\\left(\\pi_2(x)=|\\{p\\in\\mathbb N:p\\leq x\\land\\operatorname{TwinPrimePair}_S(p,p+2)\\}|\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}twin\\text{-}prime\\text{-}count} \\vdash \\forall x\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\\left(\\pi_2(x)=|\\{p\\in\\mathbb N:p\\leq x\\land\\operatorname{TwinPrimePair}_S(p,p+2)\\}|\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}twin\\text{-}prime\\text{-}constant} \\vdash C_2\\coloneqq\\prod_{\\substack{\\ell&gt;2\\\\\\operatorname{Prime}_S(\\ell)}}\\left(1-\\frac{1}{(\\ell-1)^2}\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}twin\\text{-}prime\\text{-}constant} \\vdash C_2\\coloneqq\\prod_{\\substack{\\ell&gt;2\\\\\\operatorname{Prime}_S(\\ell)}}\\left(1-\\frac{1}{(\\ell-1)^2}\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}twin\\text{-}prime\\text{-}asymptotic} \\vdash \\operatorname{HardyLittlewoodTwinPrimeAsymptotic}_S\\leftrightarrow\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\frac{\\pi_2(x)(\\log x)^2}{2C_2x}=1\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}twin\\text{-}prime\\text{-}asymptotic} \\vdash \\operatorname{HardyLittlewoodTwinPrimeAsymptotic}_S\\leftrightarrow\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\frac{\\pi_2(x)(\\log x)^2}{2C_2x}=1\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Twin primes: prime pairs <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(p, p+2)\">\\((p, p+2)\\)</span>; conjectured infinite</li>\n<li>The Hardy--Littlewood asymptotic is recorded as a conjectural predicate, not asserted as a theorem. With the convention above, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"C_2\\approx0.66016\">\\(C_2\\approx0.66016\\)</span> and the asymptotic carries the factor <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"2C_2\">\\(2C_2\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Polignac's conjecture: for every even <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\">\\(k\\)</span>, infinitely many prime pairs with difference <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\">\\(k\\)</span></li>\n<li>Bounded-gaps theorems do not prove the twin-prime conjecture and are not part of this definition.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Goldston, Graham, Pintz and Yıldırım</li>\n<li>Zhang, Bounded gaps between primes</li>\n<li>Polymath, Variants of the Selberg sieve</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch20/58-df-prime.md","status":"resolved","id":"3322615e4eea05e9","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-df-prime.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch20/58-df-prime.md","status":"resolved","id":"3322615e4eea05e9","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{Prime}_S$ (prime predicate, see [[../batch20/58-df-prime.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"p,q\\in\\mathbb N","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Prime}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{TwinPrimePair}_S(p,q)","display":false},{"tex":"\\pi_2(x)","display":false},{"tex":"C_2","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{HardyLittlewoodTwinPrimeAsymptotic}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}twin\\text{-}prime\\text{-}pair} \\vdash \\operatorname{TwinPrimePair}_S(p,q)\\leftrightarrow p,q\\in\\mathbb N\\land\\operatorname{Prime}_S(p)\\land\\operatorname{Prime}_S(q)\\land q=p+2","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}twin\\text{-}prime\\text{-}count} \\vdash \\forall x\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\\left(\\pi_2(x)=|\\{p\\in\\mathbb N:p\\leq x\\land\\operatorname{TwinPrimePair}_S(p,p+2)\\}|\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}twin\\text{-}prime\\text{-}constant} \\vdash C_2\\coloneqq\\prod_{\\substack{\\ell>2\\\\\\operatorname{Prime}_S(\\ell)}}\\left(1-\\frac{1}{(\\ell-1)^2}\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}twin\\text{-}prime\\text{-}asymptotic} \\vdash \\operatorname{HardyLittlewoodTwinPrimeAsymptotic}_S\\leftrightarrow\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\frac{\\pi_2(x)(\\log x)^2}{2C_2x}=1","display":true},{"tex":"(p, p+2)","display":false},{"tex":"C_2\\approx0.66016","display":false},{"tex":"2C_2","display":false},{"tex":"k","display":false},{"tex":"k","display":false}],"bytes":2042,"backlinks":[{"id":"01a9b20b9e439456","anchor":"ref-5","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"3363f2782f9bc6a1","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1334","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-twin-prime.md|58-df-twin-prime]]（batch07）"}],"outgoing":["3322615e4eea05e9"]}